1464..1537 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1538..1595 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1596..1667 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1668..1744 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1745..1821 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
1822..1896 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
1897..1975 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
1976..2018 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
